    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0942" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.011/10–446: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tittmann</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-04">October 4, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–240. Reference is made to Article I of the new
                    Haitian Constitution which states that the Island of Navassa is an integral part
                    of the territory of Haiti. Inasmuch as this Government regards Navassa as
                    falling under the sovereignty of the United States, you are requested to address
                    a note to the Haitian Government<anchor n="45" xml:id="d783-f1"/> making formal
                    reservation of the rights of the United States with regard to this Island.
                    Particular reference is made in this connection to the Department’s instruction
                    218 of August 13, 1932 and the Embassy’s despatch 489 of September 12,
                        1932,<anchor n="46" xml:id="d783-f2"/> regarding the action taken by <pb
                        facs="0943" n="925" xml:id="pg925"/> this Government with respect to the
                    Haitian Government’s claim to Navassa as expressed in Article I of the Haitian
                    Constitution of 1932.</p>
                <p>A separate communication is being sent the Embassy regarding provisions of the
                    new Haitian Constitution restricting the business and commercial activities of
                        foreigners.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d783-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
